# ${{ values.serviceName }}

${{ values.description }}

Terraform configuration for the Azure API Management instance `${{ values.serviceName }}`
(${{ values.sku or "Standard" }} tier, region `${{ values.location or "eastus" }}`).

## Layout

| Path | Content |
| --- | --- |
| `infra/` | Terraform root configuration |
| `infra/terraform.tfvars` | Settings of this instance |
| `infra/apis.auto.tfvars.json` | APIs published through the gateway |
| `infra/tests/` | Test that applies the configuration against mocked providers |
| `docs/` | Documentation, shown in the portal under TechDocs |
| `.github/workflows/ci.yml` | Formatting, validation, test, lint, security scan and documentation build |
| `.github/workflows/deploy.yml` | Plan and apply, skipped until Azure credentials are configured |

## Getting started

1. Read `docs/deployment.md` and configure the Azure identity and the state storage account.
2. Review `infra/terraform.tfvars` and replace the placeholder values of
   `publisher_name` and `publisher_email`.
3. Push to `main`. The Deploy workflow plans and applies the configuration.

## Local checks

```bash
cd infra
terraform fmt -check -recursive
terraform init -backend=false
terraform validate
terraform test
```

